# hs-webapp project on the self-hosted GlitchTip instance.
# Public by design -- a DSN only permits writing events.
# The key is written WITHOUT dashes: GlitchTip shows it as a dashed UUID and
# accepts either form, but the Sentry SDK parses the key as \w+ and rejects the
# dashed one outright ("Invalid Sentry Dsn"), which silently disabled reporting.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://900b1f42382e42d7897a0bcf0cbe0922@errors.hearthshelf.com/6

# Stated explicitly rather than left to the hosting dashboard. A local
# `wrangler pages deploy` does not read those dashboard variables, so a deploy
# from a workstation silently shipped the dev fallback to production. Keeping it
# in the committed production env makes every build path agree.
VITE_CONTROL_PLANE_URL=https://api.hearthshelf.com
